const SW_EDGES=[{"k":"alertness","n":"Alertness","c":"Background","s":"+2 to Notice rolls.","l":"Not much gets by this hero. He’s very observant and perceptive, and adds +2 to his Notice rolls to hear, see, or otherwise sense the world around him.","r":0,"q":[],"f":"Notice +2"},{"k":"ambidextrous","n":"Ambidextrous","c":"Background","s":"Ignore –2 penalty when making Trait rolls with off-hand.","l":"Your warrior is as deft with his left hand as he is with his right. He ignores the Off-Hand penalty (see page 104). If holding a weapon in each hand, Ambidextrous characters may stack Parry bonuses (if any) from both weapons.","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8]]},{"k":"arcane_background","n":"Arcane Background","c":"Background","s":"Allows access to the Arcane Backgrounds listed in Chapter Five.","l":"Exposure to strange energies, studies at a magical school, or gifts from divine or spiritual entities sometimes grant champions their own powers and abilities. Such events lead to the Arcane Background Edge and the development of supernatural ab","r":0,"q":[["txt","GM approval and a setting-specific arcane skill"]],"x":1,"m":1,"o":"text"},{"k":"arcane_resistance","n":"Arcane Resistance","c":"Background","s":"+2 to Trait rolls to resist magical effects; magical damage is reduced by 2.","l":"Magic and the supernatural hold little sway with this individual. Whether by nature, heritage, or training he’s particularly resistant to magic, psionics, weird science, and other supernatural energies. Arcane skills targeting the hero suffer","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8]],"f":"all rolls +2 when resisting magic"},{"k":"improved_arcane_resistance","n":"Improved Arcane Resistance","c":"Background","s":"+4 to Trait rolls to resist magical effects; magical damage is reduced by 4.","l":"As above, but the penalty to the arcane skill roll and damage are increased to 4.","r":0,"q":[["edge","arcane_resistance"]],"f":"all rolls +4 when resisting magic","sup":["arcane_resistance"]},{"k":"aristocrat","n":"Aristocrat","c":"Background","s":"+2 to Common Knowledge and networking with upper class.","l":"This individual was born into privilege or came into it later in life. She may or may not have money (the Rich or Filthy Rich Edge), but she still walks in the elite social circles of the setting. Aristocrats add +2 to Persuasion when Networking (see page 133) with the local elite, captains of industry, nobles, or other aristocrats. They also add +2 to Common Knowledge rolls made to know the etiquette of the upper class, recognize family trees or heraldry, or recall gossip concerning others of their station.","r":0,"q":[],"f":"Common Knowledge +2 when dealing with the upper class"},{"k":"attractive","n":"Attractive","c":"Background","s":"+1 to Performance and Persuasion rolls.","l":"It’s no secret people are more willing to help those they find physically attractive. Your character adds +1 to Performance and Persuasion rolls if the target is attracted to his or her general type (gender, sex, species, etc.).","r":0,"q":[["at","vigor",6]],"f":"Performance/Persuasion +1"},{"k":"very_attractive","n":"Very Attractive","c":"Background","s":"+2 to Performance and Persuasion rolls.","l":"Your hero is drop-dead gorgeous. She increases her Performance and Persuasion bonus to +2.","r":0,"q":[["edge","attractive"]],"f":"Performance/Persuasion +2","sup":["attractive"]},{"k":"berserk","n":"Berserk","c":"Background","s":"After Shaken or a Wound, all melee attacks must be Wild Attacks, +2 to Toughness, ignore one level of Wound penalties, Critical Failure on Fighting roll hits random target. Lasts until there are no foes in sight or hero makes Smarts roll at –2.","l":"Berserkers become wild and nearly uncontrollable when the “red rage” takes them, but they are deadly killing machines as well! Immediately after suffering a Wound or a Shaken result (from physical damage only), your hero must make a Smarts roll or go Berserk. She cannot voluntarily fail this check. Going Berserk has the following effects: _x0084__x0084_ FURY: Every melee attack must be a Wild Attack (see page 109). She cannot use any skills that require wit or concentration (GM’s call). She may scream out threats and use Intimidation, for example. _x0084__x0084_ ENRAGED: Adrenaline and rage fuel the berserker’s muscles, adding +2 to Toughness. She ignores one level of Wound penalties (this stacks with any other abilities that reduce Wound penalties). _x0084__x0084_RECKLESS ABANDON: Anytime a berserker rolls a Critical Failure on a Fighting check, she hits a random target within range of her attack (not the intended target), friend or foe. If there are no applicable targets, the blow simply misses, smashes nearby objects, etc. The rage ends when there are no foes in sight or the berserk chooses—but in the latter case she must make a Smarts roll at −2 (as an action).","r":0,"q":[],"f":"toughness +2 when Berserk"},{"k":"brave","n":"Brave","c":"Background","s":"+2 to Fear checks and –2 to rolls on the Fear Table.","l":"Those with this Edge have learned to master their fear, or have dealt with so many horrors they’ve become jaded. These valiant explorers add +2 to Fear checks and subtract 2 from Fear Table results","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",6]],"f":"Spirit rolls +2 when making Fear checks"},{"k":"brawny","n":"Brawny","c":"Background","s":"Size (and therefore Toughness) +1. Treat Strength as one die type higher for Encumbrance and Minimum Strength to use weapons, armor, or equipment.","l":"Your bruiser is very large or very fit. Her Size increases by +1 (this increases Toughness by 1) and she treats her Strength as one die type higher when determining Encumbrance (page 67) and Minimum Strength to use armor, weapons, and equipment","r":0,"q":[["at","strength",6],["at","vigor",6]],"f":"toughness +1"},{"k":"brute","n":"Brute","c":"Background","s":"Link Athletics to Strength instead of Agility. This includes resisting Athletics Tests as well.","l":"Brutes focus on core strength and fitness over coordination and flexibility. They treat Athletics as linked to Strength instead of Agility for purposes of Advancement. The character may also resist Athletics Tests with Strength if she chooses. F","r":0,"q":[["at","strength",6]]},{"k":"charismatic","n":"Charismatic","c":"Background","s":"Reroll a Persuasion roll as long as it’s not a Critical Failure.","l":"Your hero is likable for some reason. She may be trustworthy or kind, or might just exude confidence and goodwill. You may Reroll immediately after failing a Persuasion roll that’s not a Critical Failure","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8]]},{"k":"elan","n":"Elan","c":"Background","s":"+2 when spending a Benny to reroll a Trait roll.","l":"Elan is a French word that means energy or spirit. Those who have it rise to the occasion when the going gets toughest. When you spend a Benny to reroll a Trait, add +2 to the total. The bonus applies only when rerolling. It doesn’t apply to dam","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8]]},{"k":"fame","n":"Fame","c":"Background","s":"+1 Persuasion rolls when recognized (Common Knowledge), double usual fee for Performance.","l":"Your character is a minor celebrity of some sort. She might be a popular bard known in a particular fiefdom, a minor rock star, or a beloved B-movie actor. She makes double the normal fee when performing for pay. She can also use her celebrity t","r":0,"q":[],"f":"Persuasion +1 when recognized"},{"k":"famous","n":"Famous","c":"Background","s":"+2 Persuasion when recognized, 5× or more usual fee for Performance.","l":"Your hero is truly famous. She’s wellknown in a large circle such as a country, a large industry, or a popular medium (film or television, the music industry). She makes 5× the normal fee when performing and adds +2 to Persuasion rolls when inf","r":0,"q":[["edge","fame"]],"f":"Persuasion +2 when recognized","sup":["fame"]},{"k":"fast_healer","n":"Fast Healer","c":"Background","s":"+2 Vigor when rolling for natural healing.","l":"Those with this blessing add +2 to Vigor rolls for natural healing, and check every three days instead of five","r":0,"q":[["at","vigor",8]],"f":"Vigor rolls +2 when rolling for natural healing"},{"k":"fleet_footed","n":"Fleet-Footed","c":"Background","s":"Pace +2, increase running die one step.","l":"The hero’s Pace is increased by +2 and his running die increases one step (from d6 to d8, for example).","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",6]],"f":"pace +2"},{"k":"linguist","n":"Linguist","c":"Background","s":"Character has d6 in languages equal to half her Smarts die.","l":"This world-traveler has an ear for languages. She begins play knowing half her Smarts die type in different Language skills of her choice at d6","r":0,"q":[["at","smarts",6]],"o":"text"},{"k":"luck","n":"Luck","c":"Background","s":"+1 Benny at the start of each session.","l":"The adventurer seems to be blessed by fate, karma, the gods, or whatever external forces he believes in (or believe in him!). He draws one extra Benny at the beginning of each game session, allowing him to succeed at important tasks more often t","r":0,"q":[],"f":"bennies +1"},{"k":"great_luck","n":"Great Luck","c":"Background","s":"+2 Bennies at the start of each session.","l":"The player draws two extra Bennies instead of one at the start of each session.","r":0,"q":[["edge","luck"]],"f":"bennies +2","sup":["luck"]},{"k":"quick","n":"Quick","c":"Background","s":"Action Card must be higher than a Five.","l":"Quick characters have lightning-fast reflexes and a cool head. Whenever you are dealt an Action Card of Five or lower, you may discard it and draw again until you get a card higher than Five. Characters with both the Level Headed and Quick Edge","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8],["not","hesitant"]],"f":"initiative quick"},{"k":"rich","n":"Rich","c":"Background","s":"Character starts with three times the starting funds and a $150K annual salary.","l":"Whether the individual was born with a silver spoon in his mouth or earned it through hard work, he’s got more money than most. Rich heroes start with three times the normal starting funds for the setting. If a regular income is appropriate","r":0,"q":[]},{"k":"filthy_rich","n":"Filthy Rich","c":"Background","s":"Five times starting funds and $500K average salary.","l":"This fortunate individual is very wealthy. He has five times the starting funds for the setting during character creation and, if appropriate, a yearly income after responsibilities of around $500,000. Even wealthier characters may exist, but","r":0,"q":[["edge","rich"]]},{"k":"block","n":"Block","c":"Combat","s":"+1 Parry, ignore 1 point of Gang Up bonus.","l":"Through hard-fought experience your hero has learned to defend himself in vicious hand-to-hand combat. His Parry increases by +1 (armed or unarmed) and any Gang Up bonus against him is reduced by 1.","r":1,"q":[["sk","Fighting",8]],"f":"parry +1"},{"k":"improved_block","n":"Improved Block","c":"Combat","s":"+2 Parry, ignore 2 points of Gang Up bonus.","l":"The hero’s Parry bonus is now +2 and the Gang Up bonus against him is reduced by 2, when armed.","r":2,"q":[["edge","block"]],"f":"parry +2","sup":["block"]},{"k":"brawler","n":"Brawler","c":"Combat","s":"Toughness +1, add d4 to unarmed damage or increase it a step if combined with Martial Artist, Claws, etc.","l":"His fists hit like hammers or his talons cut like scythes. His body feels like it’s made of stone. Brawlers increase their Toughness by 1 and get a d4 damage die when causing unarmed damage (thus doing Str+d4). If they already have a damage die","r":0,"q":[["at","strength",8],["at","vigor",8]],"f":"toughness +1"},{"k":"bruiser","n":"Bruiser","c":"Combat","s":"Increase unarmed Strength damage a die type and Toughness another +1.","l":"The fighter hits even harder and his body can take even more punishment. He increases his unarmed damage die another die type and his Toughness an additional +1.","r":1,"q":[["edge","brawler"]],"f":"toughness +1"},{"k":"calculating","n":"Calculating","c":"Combat","s":"Ignore up to 2 points of penalties on one action with an Action Card of Five or less.","l":"A few seconds to study your foe’s actions gives your hero a major advantage. When his Action Card is a Five or less, he ignores up to 2 points of penalties on one action that turn, which can include Multi-Action, cover, Range, and even Wound pen","r":0,"q":[["at","smarts",8]]},{"k":"combat_reflexes","n":"Combat Reflexes","c":"Combat","s":"+2 Spirit to recover from being Shaken.","l":"Your warrior recovers quickly from shock and trauma. He adds +2 to his rolls when attempting to recover from being Shaken or Stunned.","r":1,"q":[],"f":"Spirit rolls +2 when recovering from Shaken"},{"k":"counterattack","n":"Counterattack","c":"Combat","s":"Free attack against one foe per turn who failed a Fighting roll.","l":"Fighters with this Edge deal instant punishment for an enemy’s mistakes. Once per turn (if not Shaken or Stunned), the character receives a Free Attack (page 101) against one failed Fighting attack against him. The counterattack takes place imme","r":1,"q":[["sk","Fighting",8]]},{"k":"improved_counterattack","n":"Improved Counterattack","c":"Combat","s":"As Counterattack, but against three foes per turn.","l":"As above but the hero gets a Free Attack against up to three failed attacks each turn.","r":2,"q":[["edge","counterattack"]]},{"k":"dead_shot","n":"Dead Shot","c":"Combat","s":"Once per turn, double damage from Athletics (throwing) or Shooting roll when dealt a Joker.","l":"When your Action Card is a Joker, double the total damage of your first successful Athletics (throwing) or Shooting roll this round.","r":1,"q":[["any",[["sk","Athletics",8],["sk","Shooting",8]]]]},{"k":"dodge","n":"Dodge","c":"Combat","s":"–2 to be hit by ranged attacks.","l":"The hero can anticipate attacks or move erratically under fire. Unless the victim of a surprise attack and taken completely unaware, Dodge subtracts 2 from all ranged attacks made against the character. Dodge does not stack with actual cover, ho","r":1,"q":[["at","agility",8]]},{"k":"improved_dodge","n":"Improved Dodge","c":"Combat","s":"The hero may Evade any area effect attack.","l":"The hero may Evade any area effect attack, even those that don’t normally allow it such as the blast power.","r":2,"q":[["edge","dodge"]]},{"k":"double_tap","n":"Double Tap","c":"Combat","s":"+1 to hit and damage when firing no more than RoF 1 per action.","l":"Experienced firearms experts fire two shots in rapid succession without spoiling their aim. Double Tap can only be used with weapons that have a Rate of Fire of 1 and can fire two shots without needing to manually reload. It adds +1 to hit and d","r":1,"q":[["sk","Shooting",6]],"f":"Shooting +1 when firing RoF 1 or less\ndamage +1 when firing RoF 1 or less"},{"k":"extraction","n":"Extraction","c":"Combat","s":"One adjacent foe doesn’t get a free attack when you withdraw from close combat.","l":"When a character withdraws from melee, adjacent attackers get a free Fighting attack against him. This is a very dangerous proposition for most, but not your wily champion. When moving away from adjacent foes, one of them (player’s choice), doe","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8]]},{"k":"improved_extraction","n":"Improved Extraction","c":"Combat","s":"Three adjacent foes don’t get free attacks when you withdraw from combat.","l":"Up to three foes’ attacks (player’s choice) are negated when your warrior moves out of melee with them.","r":2,"q":[["edge","extraction"]]},{"k":"feint","n":"Feint","c":"Combat","s":"You may choose to make foe resist with Smarts instead of Agility during a Fighting Test.","l":"When performing a Test (page 108) with the Fighting skill, you can choose to make the foe resist with Smarts instead of Agility.","r":0,"q":[["sk","Fighting",8]]},{"k":"first_strike","n":"First Strike","c":"Combat","s":"Free Fighting attack once per round when foe moves adjacent to you.","l":"Once per round, as long as he’s not Shaken or Stunned, the hero gets a free Fighting attack against a foe who moves adjacent to him. This automatically interrupts the opponent’s action.","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8]]},{"k":"improved_first_strike","n":"Improved First Strike","c":"Combat","s":"Free Fighting attack against up to three foes when they move adjacent.","l":"As above but the hero gets a free attack against up to three foes who move adjacent to him each turn.","r":3,"q":[["edge","first_strike"]]},{"k":"free_runner","n":"Free Runner","c":"Combat","s":"Ignore Difficult Ground and add +2 to Athletics in foot chases.","l":"Your character practices “parkour” or is just very skilled at running, jumping, swinging, scampering up walls, and over obstacles. As long as there are obstacles she can bound on, bounce off, or swing on, she ignores Difficult Ground penalties w","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8],["sk","Athletics",6]],"f":"Athletics +2 in foot chases"},{"k":"frenzy","n":"Frenzy","c":"Combat","s":"Roll a second Fighting die with one melee attack per turn.","l":"A character with Frenzy rolls a second Fighting die with any one of his Fighting attacks for the turn. The extra die is subject to all the same modifiers as the first, may be allocated to the same or different targets as he sees fit, and if it h","r":1,"q":[["sk","Fighting",8]]},{"k":"improved_frenzy","n":"Improved Frenzy","c":"Combat","s":"Roll a second Fighting die with up to two melee attacks per turn.","l":"The fighter rolls an extra Fighting die with up to two Fighting attacks in the same turn.","r":2,"q":[["edge","frenzy"]]},{"k":"giant_killer","n":"Giant Killer","c":"Combat","s":"+1d6 damage vs. creatures three Sizes larger or more.","l":"The bigger they are, the harder they are to kill. At least for most. But your hero knows how to find the weak points in the most massive of foes. Your fighter adds +1d6 damage when attacking creatures who are three or more Sizes larger than hims","r":2,"q":[]},{"k":"hard_to_kill","n":"Hard to Kill","c":"Combat","s":"Ignore Wound penalties when making Vigor rolls to avoid Bleeding Out.","l":"This adventurer has more lives than a herd of cats. He may ignore his Wound penalties when making Vigor rolls to avoid Bleeding Out","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8]]},{"k":"harder_to_kill","n":"Harder to Kill","c":"Combat","s":"Roll a die if the character perishes. Even if he’s Incapacitated, he survives somehow.","l":"Your hero is tougher to kill than Rasputin. If he is ever “killed,” roll a die. On an odd result, he’s dead as usual. On an even roll, he’s Incapacitated but somehow escapes death. He may be captured, stripped of all his belongings, or mistakenl","r":2,"q":[["edge","hard_to_kill"]]},{"k":"improvisational_fighter","n":"Improvisational Fighter","c":"Combat","s":"Ignore penalties to attack and Parry when using Improvised weapons.","l":"Heroes often find themselves fighting with pieces of equipment or furnishings not designed for combat. A brawler with this Edge has a knack for using such improvised weapons. He ignores penalties to attack and Parry when wielding them.","r":1,"q":[["at","smarts",6]]},{"k":"iron_jaw","n":"Iron Jaw","c":"Combat","s":"+2 to Soak and Vigor rolls to avoid Knockout Blows.","l":"The hero can shrug off even extreme blows. He adds +2 to Soak rolls and Vigor rolls to avoid Knockout Blows","r":0,"q":[["at","vigor",8]],"f":"Vigor rolls +2 when Soaking or avoiding a Knockout Blow"},{"k":"killer_instinct","n":"Killer Instinct","c":"Combat","s":"Win tied opposed rolls and may spend Bennies (or Conviction if used) to increase total after defender declares total.","l":"This hero hates losing. If he ties on an opposed roll, he wins. If he loses an opposed roll he initiated, he gets a Reroll after the defender rolls. This occurs after the defender gets his total, so the defender may not spend Bennies to adjust it","r":1,"q":[]},{"k":"level_headed","n":"Level Headed","c":"Combat","s":"Draw an additional Action Card each round and choose which one to use.","l":"Fighters who can keep their cool when everyone else is running for cover make deadly combatants. A hero with this Edge draws an additional Action Card in combat and chooses which to use.","r":1,"q":[["at","smarts",8],["not","hesitant"]],"f":"cards +1"},{"k":"improved_level_headed","n":"Improved Level Headed","c":"Combat","s":"Draw three Action Cards each round and choose which one to use.","l":"As above but the hero draws three cards and chooses the one he wants to keep.","r":1,"q":[["edge","level_headed"]],"f":"cards +2","sup":["level_headed"]},{"k":"marksman","n":"Marksman","c":"Combat","s":"Ignore up to 2 points of Athletics (throwing) or Shooting penalties when not moving and firing no more than RoF 1 per action.","l":"The hero is a natural with ranged weapons. If she doesn’t move in a turn and fires no more than a Rate of Fire of 1 per action, she may ignore up to 2 points of Athletics (throwing) or Shooting penalties from Called Shots, cover, Range, or Size.","r":1,"q":[["any",[["sk","Athletics",8],["sk","Shooting",8]]]]},{"k":"martial_artist","n":"Martial Artist","c":"Combat","s":"Unarmed Fighting +1, ignore Unarmed Defender rule, add d4 damage die to unarmed Fighting attacks (or increase die a step if you already have it).","l":"The fighter has trained in basic martial arts. When unarmed, she adds +1 to Fighting attacks and does Str+d4 damage (or increases her damage a die type if she already has it from another source, such as Claws or the Brawler Edge). Her hands coun","r":0,"q":[["sk","Fighting",6]],"f":"Fighting +1 when fighting unarmed"},{"k":"martial_warrior","n":"Martial Warrior","c":"Combat","s":"Unarmed Fighting +2, increase damage die type a step.","l":"The warrior is well on her way to becoming a martial arts master. Her unarmed combat damage increases a die type and she adds +2 to unarmed Fighting attacks.","r":1,"q":[["edge","martial_artist"]],"f":"Fighting +2 when fighting unarmed","sup":["martial_artist"]},{"k":"mighty_blow","n":"Mighty Blow","c":"Combat","s":"Once per turn, double Fighting damage when dealt a Joker.","l":"If your Action Card is a Joker, double the damage of your first successful Fighting attack that round.","r":1,"q":[["sk","Fighting",8]]},{"k":"nerves_of_steel","n":"Nerves of Steel","c":"Combat","s":"Ignore one level of Wound penalties.","l":"Your hero has learned to fight on through the most intense pain. He may ignore 1 point of Wound penalties.","r":0,"q":[["at","vigor",8]],"f":"ignore wounds +1"},{"k":"improved_nerves_of_steel","n":"Improved Nerves of Steel","c":"Combat","s":"Ignore up to two levels of Wound penalties.","l":"The hero ignores two points of Wound penalties.","r":0,"q":[["edge","nerves_of_steel"]],"f":"ignore wounds +2","sup":["nerves_of_steel"]},{"k":"no_mercy","n":"No Mercy","c":"Combat","s":"+2 damage when spending a Benny to reroll damage.","l":"When this killer spends a Benny to reroll damage, he adds +2 to his final total.","r":1,"q":[],"f":"damage +2 when spending a Benny to reroll damage"},{"k":"rapid_fire","n":"Rapid Fire","c":"Combat","s":"Increase RoF by 1 for one Shooting attack per turn.","l":"The shooter is practiced at taking quick and accurate shots. As long as she’s armed with a fast-firing ranged weapon of some sort (such as a revolver or semi-automatic) and has enough bullets to do so, she may increase her weapon’s Rate of Fire","r":1,"q":[["sk","Shooting",6]]},{"k":"improved_rapid_fire","n":"Improved Rapid Fire","c":"Combat","s":"Increase RoF by 1 for up to two Shooting attacks per turn.","l":"The shooter may now increase her weapon’s Rate of Fire by 1 twice in the same turn (via a Multi-Action).","r":2,"q":[["edge","rapid_fire"]]},{"k":"rock_and_roll","n":"Rock and Roll!","c":"Combat","s":"Ignore the Recoil penalty when firing weapons with a RoF of 2 or more.","l":"Experienced shooters learn to compensate for the recoil of fully automatic weapons. If a character with this Edge doesn’t move on his turn, he ignores the Recoil penalty when firing at a Rate of Fire of 2 or higher.","r":1,"q":[["sk","Shooting",8]]},{"k":"steady_hands","n":"Steady Hands","c":"Combat","s":"Ignore Unstable Platform penalty; reduce running penalty to –1.","l":"Firing from the back of a horse or moving vehicle is tricky business, but your adventurer has figured it out. She ignores the Unstable Platform penalty (see page 109). This also helps when running, reducing the usual penalty from –2 to ?1","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8]]},{"k":"sweep","n":"Sweep","c":"Combat","s":"Fighting roll at –2 to hit all targets in weapon’s Reach, no more than once per turn.","l":"Sweep allows a character to make a single Fighting attack and apply it against all targets in his weapon’s Reach at a ?2 penalty (friends and foes alike). Resolve damage separately for each enemy that’s hit. A fighter may only perform a Sweep on","r":0,"q":[["at","strength",8],["sk","Fighting",8]]},{"k":"improved_sweep","n":"Improved Sweep","c":"Combat","s":"As above, but ignore the –2 penalty.","l":"As above but the whirlwind of death may ignore the ?2 penalty.","r":2,"q":[["edge","sweep"]]},{"k":"trademark_weapon","n":"Trademark Weapon","c":"Combat","s":"+1 to Athletics (throwing), Fighting, or Shooting total with a specific weapon; +1 Parry while weapon is readied.","l":"The hero knows one unique weapon (Excalibur, Old Betsy, Sting) like the back of his hand. When using it, he adds +1 to his Athletics (throwing), Fighting, or Shooting rolls, and +1 to Parry when readied (even if it’s a ranged weapon). A fighter","r":0,"q":[["any",[["sk","Fighting",8],["sk","Shooting",8],["sk","Athletics",8]]]],"f":"Athletics/Fighting/Shooting +1 when using the trademark weapon\nparry +1 when the trademark weapon is readied","o":"text"},{"k":"improved_trademark_weapon","n":"Improved Trademark Weapon","c":"Combat","s":"The bonus increases to +2.","l":"As above but the bonuses when using the weapon increase to +2.","r":2,"q":[["edge","trademark_weapon"]],"f":"Athletics/Fighting/Shooting +2 when using the trademark weapon\nparry +1 when the trademark weapon is readied","sup":["trademark_weapon"]},{"k":"two_fisted","n":"Two-Fisted","c":"Combat","s":"Wielding two melee weapons, make one extra Fighting roll with second weapon at no Multi-Action penalty.","l":"If a character attacks with a melee weapon in one action and a second Off-Hand (page 104) melee weapon in a later action, the second attack doesn’t inflict a Multi-Action penalty. The Off-Hand penalty still applies unless he’s Ambidextrous, howe","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8]]},{"k":"two_gun_kid","n":"Two-Gun Kid","c":"Combat","s":"Wielding two ranged weapons, make one extra Shooting roll with second weapon at no Multi-Action penalty.","l":"If a character attacks with a ranged weapon in one action and a second “Off-Hand” ranged weapon in a later action, the second attack doesn’t inflict a Multi-Action penalty. The Off-Hand penalty still applies unless he’s Ambidextrous, however. I","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8]]},{"k":"command","n":"Command","c":"Leadership","s":"+1 to recover from being Shaken for troops in command.","l":"Command is the basic ability to give clear instructions and support to allies in the thick of battle. Extras in Command Range add +1 to their Spirit rolls when attempting to recover from being Shaken.","r":0,"q":[["at","smarts",6]],"x":1},{"k":"command_presence","n":"Command Presence","c":"Leadership","s":"Increase Command Range to 10” (20 yards)","l":"A booming voice, effective commands, natural charisma, or simple training results in a much more effective combat element. A hero with this Edge has a Command Range of 10” (20 yards).","r":0,"q":[["edge","command"]],"x":1},{"k":"fervor","n":"Fervor","c":"Leadership","s":"+1 to Extras’ Fighting rolls in Command Range.","l":"A simple phrase uttered by a great leader can sometimes have momentous results. A commander with this ability can inspire his troops to bloody fervor by yelling a motto, slogan, or other inspirational words. Extras in range add +1 to their Fighting damage rolls.","r":1,"q":[["at","spirit",8],["edge","command"]],"x":1},{"k":"hold_the_line","n":"Hold the Line","c":"Leadership","s":"+1 to Extras’ Toughness in Command Range.","l":"Hold the Line strengthens the will of any Extras under the hero’s command, adding +1 to their Toughness.","r":0,"q":[["at","smarts",8],["edge","command"]],"x":1},{"k":"inspire","n":"Inspire","c":"Leadership","s":"Once per turn, the hero may roll his Battle skill to Support one type of Trait roll, and apply it to everyone in Command Range","l":"Exceptional leaders inspire those around them to great feats of valor and determination. Once per turn, the hero may roll his Battle skill to Support one type of Trait roll, and apply it to everyone in Command Range. A leader could Support all Shooting attacks in range, for example, or all Spirit rolls to recover from being Shaken.","r":1,"q":[["edge","command"]],"x":1},{"k":"natural_leader","n":"Natural Leader","c":"Leadership","s":"Leadership Edges that apply to Extras now apply to Wild Cards as well.","l":"This leader has proven herself time and time again, gaining the respect of all those who fight by her side. Any Leadership Edge that says it applies only to Extras now applies to Wild Cards as well.","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8],["edge","command"]],"x":1},{"k":"tactician","n":"Tactician","c":"Leadership","s":"Draw an extra Action Card each turn that may be assigned to any ally in Command Range.","l":"The commander has a natural grasp of small unit tactics and can take advantage of rapidly changing situations. A Tactician is dealt an extra Action Card each turn—kept separate from his own cards. At the start of the round, he may discard it or give it to any one allied Extra or Wild Card in Command Range. The player or GM controlling the receiving character can decide whether to accept and replace her current Action Card, or discard it.","r":2,"q":[["at","smarts",8],["edge","command"]],"x":1},{"k":"master_tactician","n":"Master Tactician","c":"Leadership","s":"Draw and distribute two extra Action Cards instead of one.","l":"The Tactician now gets a total of two extra Action Cards to distribute each turn.","r":3,"q":[["at","smarts",8],["edge","tactician"]],"x":1},{"k":"artificer","n":"Artificer","c":"Power","s":"Allows user to create Arcane Devices.","l":"Those who tangle with supernatural forces sometimes find ways to imbue powers into items. They may turn an ordinary blade into a magic sword, brew a potion that can heal an ally’s Wounds, or even bless a holy relic with divine grace. Artificers can create wondrous items and devices using the Arcane Devices system","r":0,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"]],"x":1},{"k":"channeling","n":"Channeling","c":"Power","s":"Reduce Power Point cost by 1 with a raise on the activation roll.","l":"When the character gets a raise on her arcane skill roll, she reduces its Power Point cost by 1. This can take it to 0.","r":1,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"]],"x":1},{"k":"concentration","n":"Concentration","c":"Power","s":"Shaken results don’t cause Disruption (only Stun or Wounds).","l":"The caster has learned to concentrate through mild injury or setbacks. He doesn’t have to make a Smarts roll to keep his powers active when Shaken. He checks only when he’s Stunned or Wounded","r":1,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"]],"x":1},{"k":"extra_effort","n":"Extra Effort","c":"Power","s":"Increase Focus by +1 for 1 Power Point or +2 for 3 Power Points.","l":"Some Gifted can dig deep into their souls to significantly boost their powers. Extra Effort increases a Focus total after it’s rolled by +1 for 1 Power Point, or +2 for 3 Power Points. It may not be used to improve a Critical Failure.","r":1,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"]],"x":1},{"k":"gadgeteer","n":"Gadgeteer","c":"Power","s":"Build gadgets that imitate powers (Weird Science).","l":"Some mechanical gurus can build incredible devices out of most anything. A Gadgeteer can spend up to three Power Points to “jury rig” a device from most any reasonable collection of spare parts. This allows her to use any power normally available to Weird Scientists of her Rank or lower in her particular setting. The total cost of the power cannot exceed the points spent to create it. This takes one entire turn, during which she can do nothing else but make a Weird Science roll at ?2 (she cannot take Multi-Actions that round). The inventor uses Power Points directly from her pool for the device, but once its initial Duration is finished it falls apart into its component pieces.","r":0,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"],["sk","Weird Science",8]],"x":1},{"k":"holy_unholy_warrior","n":"Holy/Unholy Warrior","c":"Power","s":"Add +1 to +4 to Soak rolls for each Power Point spent.","l":"Believers face grave dangers in service to their divine patrons. To survive such hardships, the forces of good (or evil) grant miracles and the ability to turn their favor into supernatural protection. The chosen may add +1 to the total of a final Soak roll for each Power Point spent, to a maximum of 4.","r":1,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"],["sk","Faith",6]],"x":1},{"k":"mentalist","n":"Mentalist","c":"Power","s":"+2 to opposed Psionics rolls.","l":"Constant contact with multiple minds gives these psionic agents an edge when it comes to forcing or resisting mental assaults. Mentalists add +2 to opposed Psionics rolls, whether they are using their powers against a foe or defending against a rival. The bonus doesn’t apply to members of other species (animals, aliens, etc.).","r":0,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"],["sk","Psionics",6]],"x":1,"f":"Psionics +2 when in opposed Psionics rolls"},{"k":"new_powers","n":"New Powers","c":"Power","s":"Your character knows two new powers.","l":"An arcane character may learn two new powers by choosing this Edge (which may be taken multiple times). He may choose from any powers of his Rank or lower normally available to his particular Arcane Background.","r":0,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"]],"x":1,"m":1,"o":"text"},{"k":"power_points","n":"Power Points","c":"Power","s":"Gain 5 additional Power Points, no more than once per Rank.","l":"Wizards, weird scientists, and other arcane types always want more power. This Edge grants them an additional 5 Power Points. Power Points may be selected more than once, but only once per Rank. It may be taken as often as desired at Legendary Rank, but each grants only 2 additional points.","r":0,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"]],"x":1,"f":"pp +5","m":1,"o":"text"},{"k":"power_surge","n":"Power Surge","c":"Power","s":"Recover 10 Power Points when dealt a Joker in combat.","l":"The character recovers 10 Power Points when his Action Card is a Joker. This may not exceed his usual limit.","r":1,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"]],"x":1},{"k":"rapid_recharge","n":"Rapid Recharge","c":"Power","s":"Recover 10 Power Points per hour.","l":"Power Points normally recharge at a rate of 5 points every hour spent resting (see Recharging, page 150). This Edge doubles that rate to 10 every hour.","r":1,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"],["at","spirit",6]],"x":1},{"k":"improved_rapid_recharge","n":"Improved Rapid Recharge","c":"Power","s":"Recover 20 Power Points per hour.","l":"The character now regains 20 Power Points per hour spent resting.","r":2,"q":[["edge","rapid_recharge"]],"x":1},{"k":"soul_drain","n":"Soul Drain","c":"Power","s":"Recover 5 Power Points for a level of Fatigue.","l":"Desperate times call for desperate measures. Soul Drain allows an arcane character to channel her physical energy into power, taking a level of Fatigue in exchange for 5 Power Points (she can also Exhaust herself for 10 Power Points).","r":1,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"]],"x":1},{"k":"wizard","n":"Wizard","c":"Power","s":"Spend 1 extra Power Point to change a spell’s Trapping.","l":"Magic is varied and wonderful, and wizards are exposed to countless tomes, scrolls, and incantations as they master their craft. Sometimes they use this knowledge to recall variations of their various enchantments. A Wizard can spend 1 extra Power Point when casting a power to change its Trapping. A fireball (blast) might manifest as a lightning bolt, for example. This can often have important consequences if a foe has a particular resistance or weakness to the spell’s usual Trapping.","r":1,"q":[["edge","arcane_background"],["sk","Spellcasting",10]],"x":1},{"k":"ace","n":"Ace","c":"Professional","s":"Character may spend Bennies to Soak damage for his vehicle. May Reroll failed maneuver roll due to a Complication.","l":"Aces are pilots and drivers who have a special affinity with their car, boat, plane, or other vehicle. They may spend Bennies to make Soak rolls for a vehicle they control or command, using Boating, Driving, or Piloting instead of Vigor. Each success and raise negates a Wound and any associated Critical Hit (see page 119). Aces also get to Reroll if they fail a maneuvering roll due to a Complication","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8]],"x":1},{"k":"acrobat","n":"Acrobat","c":"Professional","s":"–1 to hit character if she has no Encumbrance or Minimum Strength penalties.","l":"Nimble fighters are able to leap about their foes, confusing them and making them harder to hit with ranged and melee attacks. Attacks against the Acrobat are made at ?1 as long as he’s aware of his attacker, can reasonably move about, and isn’t suffering any Encumbrance or Minimum Strength penalties.","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8],["sk","Athletics",8]],"x":1},{"k":"assassin","n":"Assassin","c":"Professional","s":"+2 to damage foes when Vulnerable or assassin has The Drop.","l":"Assassins are trained killers who know how to kill even the toughest foes. They add +2 to damage rolls when their foe is Vulnerable or they have The Drop.","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8],["sk","Fighting",6],["sk","Stealth",8]],"x":1,"f":"damage +2 when the target is Vulnerable or you have The Drop"},{"k":"investigator","n":"Investigator","c":"Professional","s":"+2 to Research and certain types of Notice rolls.","l":"Investigators spend a great deal of time researching ancient legends, working the streets, or deducing devilish mysteries. Some of these heroes are actual private investigators while others are sleuthing mages in a fantasy world or inquisitive college professors stumbling upon Things Man Was Not Meant to Know. Investigators add +2 to Research rolls and Notice rolls made to search through desks for important papers, sift through stacks of junk mail for something of note, or spy obscured items from piles of junk or debris.","r":0,"q":[["at","smarts",8],["sk","Research",8]],"x":1,"f":"Research +2\nNotice +2 when investigating"},{"k":"jack_of_all_trades","n":"Jack-of-all-Trades","c":"Professional","s":"With a Smarts roll and an hour’s study, gain d4 in a skill (or d6 with a raise) until the session ends.","l":"Through advanced schooling, book-learning, computer-enhanced skill programs, or just amazing intuitive perception, your hero has a talent for picking up skills on the fly. There’s little he can’t figure out given a little time and a dash of luck. The character makes a Smarts roll after an hour of study or immersion on a particular skill. With success, she gains a d4 in the skill, or d6 with a raise. She may spend another hour studying to try again if she likes to get a raise. This lasts until the character studies a different subject. The Edge may not be used to increase a skill she actually has points in.","r":0,"q":[["at","smarts",10]],"x":1},{"k":"mcgyver","n":"McGyver","c":"Professional","s":"Quickly create improvised devices from scraps.","l":"A McGyver can improvise a device from common resources when the need arises. Given a few simple items, he can make a Repair roll to craft improvised weapons, explosives, or tools, that last until used or the end of the encounter (GM’s call). Failure means he can’t find the required components but can try again next round. A Critical Failure means he’s out of luck and can’t create the tool this encounter. Success creates a minor explosive (2d4 explosive in a Small Blast Template), a one shot projectile weapon like a “zip gun” (Range 5/10/20, Damage 2d6), rickety raft, electrical source, etc. A raise creates a larger explosive (2d6 in a Medium Blast Template or 2d4 in a Large), ranged weapon with a few more shots, 2d8 damage or twice the range, a more stable raft, a more powerful battery, etc. The quality or power of the creation is completely up to the Game Master, but creativity should be rewarded, particularly in the most dire and dramatic situations.","r":0,"q":[["at","smarts",6],["sk","Repair",8],["sk","Notice",8]],"x":1},{"k":"mr_fix_it","n":"Mr. Fix It","c":"Professional","s":"+2 to Repair rolls, half the time required with a raise.","l":"The mechanic adds +2 to Repair rolls. With a raise, he halves the time normally required to fix something. This means if a particular Repair job says a raise repairs it in half the time, a Mr. Fix It could finish the job in onequarter the time with a raise.","r":0,"q":[["sk","Repair",8]],"x":1,"f":"Repair +2"},{"k":"scholar","n":"Scholar","c":"Professional","s":"+2 to any one “knowledge” skill.","l":"Learned professors, devoted students, and amateur enthusiasts spend great amounts of time and energy studying particular subjects. They become experts in these fields, and rarely fail to answer questions in their particular area of expertise. Pick any one of the following skills: Academics, Battle, Occult, Science, or a Smarts-based “knowledge”-type skill allowed in your setting, and add +2 to the total whenever they’re used. This Edge may be taken more than once if applied to different skills.","r":0,"q":[],"f":"$skill +2","m":1,"o":"skill"},{"k":"soldier","n":"Soldier","c":"Professional","s":"Treat Minimum Strength as one die type higher for Encumbrance and Min Str. May Reroll Vigor rolls when resisting environmental Hazards.","l":"Professional soldiers get used to carrying heavy loads, and enduring harsh conditions. After a few days getting used to their gear (GM’s call), they treat their Strength as one die type higher when determining Encumbrance and Minimum Strength to use armor, weapons, and equipment without a penalty. (This stacks with the Brawny Edge.) They also Reroll Vigor rolls made to survive environmental hazards","r":0,"q":[["at","strength",6],["at","vigor",6]],"x":1},{"k":"thief","n":"Thief","c":"Professional","s":"+1 Thievery, Athletics rolls made to climb, Stealth in urban environments.","l":"Thieves specialize in deceit, treachery, and acrobatics. They can be invaluable where traps must be detected, walls must be climbed, and locks must be picked. Thieves know how to use protrusions on walls and window ledges to climb the tallest of buildings, scampering through streets and back alleys like cats. They add +1 to Athletics rolls made to climb in urban areas. Thieves also know how to use the dark areas between the streetlights of cities to conceal their movements, and add +1 to Stealth rolls when in an urban environment. Finally, these rogues are—not surprisingly— adept at Thievery itself, adding +1 to those rolls in all circumstances.","r":0,"q":[["at","agility",8],["sk","Stealth",6],["sk","Thievery",6]],"x":1,"f":"Thievery +1\nAthletics +1 when climbing\nStealth +1 in urban areas"},{"k":"woodsman","n":"Woodsman","c":"Professional","s":"+2 to Survival and Stealth in the wilds.","l":"Woodsmen are rangers, scouts, and hunters who are more at home in the wilderness than in urban areas. They are skilled trackers and scouts, and know how to live off the land for months at a time. Woodsmen add +2 to Survival rolls, and Stealth rolls made in the wild (not towns, ruins, or underground).","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",6],["sk","Survival",8]],"x":1,"f":"Survival/Stealth +2 in the wilds"},{"k":"bolster","n":"Bolster","c":"Social","s":"May remove Distracted or Vulnerable state after a Test.","l":"Belittling or humiliating an enemy can also boost your ally’s spirits. When this character successfully Tests a foe, he may also remove the Distracted or Vulnerable state from one of his allies.","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8]],"x":1},{"k":"common_bond","n":"Common Bond","c":"Social","s":"The hero may freely give her Bennies to others.","l":"Selfless heroes and determined leaders know their greatest strength often comes from their companions, and are willing to give some of their own fortune, fate, or luck to support them. A character with this Edge may freely give her Bennies to any other character she can communicate with. The player should explain what form this takes, from a quick shout of encouragement to a welcome pat on the back.","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8]],"x":1},{"k":"connections","n":"Connections","c":"Social","s":"Contacts provide aid or other favors once per session.","l":"Your heroine is connected to people or organizations who can help her when the chips are down. It might be the mob, the Feds, a union, or even other adventurers. Connections may be taken more than once, selecting a new faction or contact each time. Once per session, and assuming she can get in touch with them, the heroine can call on her friends for a favor. The favor depends on the nature of the contact (GM’s call), but might include a loan, gear, a few allied fighters, transportation, information, or even a professional with critical skills the party doesn’t have, like a hacker or scholar.","r":0,"q":[]},{"k":"humiliate","n":"Humiliate","c":"Social","s":"Special +2 to Taunt.","l":"Likable people can build up others, giving them self-confidence and esteem. They can just as easily take it away, destroying a rival’s ego with a cruel and cutting remark. Your hero adds +2 to Taunt Tests.","r":0,"q":[],"f":"Taunt +2 when humiliating"},{"k":"menacing","n":"Menacing","c":"Social","s":"Mean or Ugly +2 to Intimidation.","l":"Being a brutish lout isn’t always a drawback if you know how to use it. Menacing allows a character to put her bad looks or worse attitude to good use. The goon adds +2 to her Intimidation rolls.","r":0,"q":[],"f":"Intimidation +2 if has mean|ugly"},{"k":"provoke","n":"Provoke","c":"Social","s":"May “provoke” foes with a raise on a Taunt roll.","l":"Clever characters can manipulate their foes, drawing enemy focus on themselves to protect their allies. Once per turn, when your hero uses Taunt for a Test and gets a raise, she may choose to make the affected target Shaken and “provoked.” Provoked enemies suffer a ?2 penalty to affect any other target besides the one who provoked her. This stacks with Distracted but not further instances of Provoke. It lasts until a Joker is drawn, someone else Provokes the target, or the encounter ends. Provoke can affect multiple targets, and may be combined with Rabble Rouser.","r":0,"q":[]},{"k":"rabble_rouser","n":"Rabble-Rouser","c":"Social","s":"Once per turn, affect all foes in a Medium Blast Template with an Intimidation or Taunt Test.","l":"This instigator knows how to rile up several enemies at once. Once per turn, a character with this Edge can make a social Test with Intimidation or Taunt against all enemies in a Medium Blast Template. The targets must be able to see and hear the hero clearly. Each defender resists and is affected by the Test separately.","r":1,"q":[["at","spirit",8]],"x":1},{"k":"reliable","n":"Reliable","c":"Social","s":"May Reroll a failed Support roll.","l":"People know they can depend on your hero when they need assistance. If he fails a Support roll, he gets a Reroll.","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8]],"x":1},{"k":"retort","n":"Retort","c":"Social","s":"A raise when resisting a Taunt or Intimidation attack makes the foe distracted","l":"This verbal duelist can turn the slings and arrows of social combat right back at the unwitting fools who hurled them. 51 Characters If a character with Retort gets a raise when resisting an Intimidation or Taunt Test, the foe is Distracted.","r":0,"q":[]},{"k":"streetwise","n":"Streetwise","c":"Social","s":"+2 to Common Knowledge and criminal networking.","l":"Streetwise characters know how to find the local black market, fence stolen goods, avoid the local law (or criminal element!), lay low when the heat’s on, obtain illegal weapons, find out which “boss” is hiring muscle, or similar shady activities. Streetwise characters add +2 to Intimidation or Persuasion rolls made to Network with shady or criminal elements. They also add +2 to Common Knowledge rolls pertaining to the types of disreputable activities listed above.","r":0,"q":[["at","smarts",6]],"x":1,"f":"Common Knowledge +2"},{"k":"strong_willed","n":"Strong Willed","c":"Social","s":"+2 to resist Smarts or Spirit-based Tests.","l":"Self-confidence is strong armor against those who would belittle this individual. He adds +2 to rolls made to resist Smarts or Spirit-based Tests.","r":0,"q":[["at","smarts",6],["at","spirit",6]],"x":1,"f":"Smarts/Spirit rolls +2 when resisting Tests"},{"k":"iron_will","n":"Iron Will","c":"Social","s":"+4 to resist Smarts or Spirit-based Tests.","l":"Few things phase this character’s powerful psyche. The bonus increases to +4.","r":1,"q":[["edge","strong_willed"]],"x":1,"f":"Smarts/Spirit rolls +4 when resisting Tests","sup":["strong_willed"]},{"k":"work_the_room","n":"Work the Room","c":"Social","s":"Once per turn, roll a second die when Supporting via Performance or Persuasion and apply result to additional ally.","l":"Once per turn, a character with this Edge rolls a second die with any one of his Support actions using Persuasion or Performance. The additional die is assigned to another ally (not the original target) who can see or hear the hero.","r":1,"q":[["at","spirit",8]],"x":1},{"k":"work_the_crowd","n":"Work the Crowd","c":"Social","s":"Work the Room As above, but up to twice per turn.","l":"As above but the hero now gains an additional die on up to two of her Support actions.","r":2,"q":[["edge","work_the_room"]],"x":1},{"k":"beast_bond","n":"Beast Bond","c":"Weird","s":"The hero may spend Bennies for animals under her control.","l":"Some individuals have an extraordinary bond with their animal companions. These characters may spend their own Bennies for any animals under their control, including mounts, pets, familiars, and so on. Beast Master","r":0,"q":[]},{"k":"champion","n":"Champion","c":"Weird","s":"Fighting d6 +2 damage vs. supernaturally evil creatures.","l":"Champions are holy (or unholy) men and women chosen to fight for a particular deity or religion. Most are pious souls ready and willing to lay down their lives for a greater cause, but some may have been born into the role and follow their path with some reluctance. Champions fight the forces of darkness (or good), adding +2 damage when attacking supernaturally evil (or good if they’re evil) creatures. The bonus applies to area effect damage, ranged attacks, powers, etc. The GM must decide which foes this bonus applies to, but generally it’s any evil (or good!) creature born of magic or with any supernatural abilities.","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8],["sk","Fighting",8]],"x":1,"f":"damage +2 against supernaturally evil creatures"},{"k":"chi","n":"Chi","c":"Weird","s":"Once per combat, reroll failed attack, make enemy reroll successful attack, or add +d6 to unarmed Fighting attack.","l":"Your hero’s martial arts training goes beyond the norm and into the realm of the mystical. At the start of each combat encounter, she gains a “Chi Point” that can be spent to: • Reroll one of her failed attacks (even a Critical Failure). • Make an enemy reroll a successful attack that was made against her. • Add +d6 damage to one of her successful unarmed Fighting attacks (this may Ace). Chi is lost at the end of the combat encounter.","r":2,"q":[]},{"k":"danger_sense","n":"Danger Sense","c":"Weird","s":"Notice roll at +2 to sense ambushes or similar events.","l":"Your hero can sense when something bad is about to happen. When he’s about to be the victim of an ambush or other surprise attack, he gets a +2 bonus to his Notice roll. With a raise, he starts the encounter on Hold. If the danger would not usually allow a Notice roll, he may still realize something is about to happen but doesn’t get the bonus.","r":0,"q":[],"f":"Notice +2 when sensing ambushes"},{"k":"healer","n":"Healer","c":"Weird","s":"+2 to Healing rolls, magical or otherwise.","l":"A hero with this Edge adds +2 to all Healing rolls, whether natural or magical in nature.","r":0,"q":[["at","spirit",8]],"x":1,"f":"Healing +2"},{"k":"liquid_courage","n":"Liquid Courage","c":"Weird","s":"Alcohol increases Vigor a die type and ignores one level of Wound penalty; –1 to Agility, Smarts, and related skills.","l":"This gregarious individual processes alcohol far differently than most. The round after consuming a stiff drink (about eight ounces of hard liquor or equivalent), her Vigor increases one die type (increasing Toughness as well). The drinker can also ignore one level of Wound penalties (which stacks with other abilities that do the same). Smarts and Agility-based rolls suffer a ?1 penalty for the duration, however. The effect lasts for one hour after it begins, at which point the boozer suffers a level of Fatigue for the next four hours.","r":0,"q":[["at","vigor",8]],"x":1},{"k":"scavenger","n":"Scavenger","c":"Weird","s":"Luck Once per session, may find a piece of necessary equipment.","l":"Once per session the hero may find, \"\"suddenly remember,\"\" or dig up some much- needed piece of equipment, a handful of ammunition, or some other useful device. The Game Master has the final word on what can and can’t be found.","r":0,"q":[]},{"k":"followers","n":"Followers","c":"Legendary","s":"The hero has five followers.","l":"Heroes often acquire dedicated warbands, \"merry men,\" or others who voluntarily follow the hero on his adventures. Each time this Edge is chosen, five followers join the hero’s band. If any are lost, others eventually take their place (how long is up to the GM and the circumstances). The followers must have some way to eat and earn income, and generally want a share of whatever loot, treasure, or other rewards the hero acquires. Otherwise, they are completely dedicated to their task. They don’t throw their lives away for no reason, but risk them repeatedly in his service. The GM determines the followers’ statistics, but in general, use the Followers statistics presented in the sidebar.","r":4,"q":[]},{"k":"professional","n":"Professional","c":"Legendary","s":"The character’s Trait and its limit increases one step.","l":"The character is an expert at a particular skill or attribute (his choice). This increases the Trait and its limit one step (a d12+1 becomes a d12+2, for example). This Edge may be selected once per Trait.","r":4,"q":[["txt","A Trait at d12"]],"x":1,"m":1,"o":"text"},{"k":"expert","n":"Expert","c":"Legendary","s":"The character’s Trait and its limit increases one step.","l":"As the Professional Edge, increasing the Trait and its limit one additional step.","r":4,"q":[["edge","professional"]],"x":1,"m":1,"o":"text"},{"k":"master","n":"Master","c":"Legendary","s":"The character’s Wild Die is a d10 with a chosen Trait.","l":"Expert in affected Trait The character’s Wild Die increases to a d10 when rolling the selected Expert Trait. It may be taken once for each.","r":4,"q":[["edge","expert"]],"x":1},{"k":"sidekick","n":"Sidekick","c":"Legendary","s":"The character gains a Wild Card sidekick.","l":"A character who triumphs over evil time and time again becomes an inspiration to others. Eventually, one of these young crusaders may attempt to join the hero in his epic quests. The hero gains a Novice ,@Rank sidekick. The sidekick is a Wild Card, gains experience as usual, and has abilities that complement or mimic his mentor. The player character should control his sidekick just like any other ally. Of course, the sidekick may occasionally cause trouble (by getting captured, running into danger when he’s not supposed to, etc.). The player should be prepared for his Edge to occasionally become a Hindrance! If the sidekick dies, he isn’t replaced unless the hero chooses this Edge again. Fortunately, heroes may always spend Bennies for their sidekicks as if she had the Common Bond Edge. Sidekicks must actually take that Edge to do the same for their mentors.","r":4,"q":[]},{"k":"tough_as_nails","n":"Tough as Nails","c":"Legendary","s":"The hero can take four Wounds before being Incapacitated.","l":"Your character keeps going when even other heroes fall. She can take four Wounds before she’s Incapacitated (her maximum Wound penalty is still ?3).","r":4,"q":[["at","vigor",12]],"x":1,"f":"max wounds +1"},{"k":"weapon_master","n":"Weapon Master","c":"Legendary","s":"Fighting d12 Parry increases by +1 and Fighting bonus damage die is d8.","l":"When armed, this legendary warrior increases his Parry by +1 and the bonus damage die for Fighting rolls is a d8.","r":4,"q":[["sk","Fighting",12]],"x":1,"f":"parry +1"},{"k":"master_of_arms","n":"Master of Arms","c":"Legendary","s":"Parry increases another +1 and Fighting bonus damage die is d10.","l":"Increase the hero’s Parry an additional +1 and his Fighting bonus damage die is now a d10.","r":4,"q":[["edge","weapon_master"]],"x":1,"f":"parry +1"}],SW_HIND=[{"k":"all_thumbs","n":"All Thumbs","kd":"m","s":"–2 to use mechanical or electrical devices.","f":"Repair/Electronics/Hacking -2 when using mechanical or electrical devices"},{"k":"anemic","n":"Anemic","kd":"m","s":"–2 Vigor when resisting Fatigue.","f":"Vigor rolls -2 when resisting Fatigue"},{"k":"arrogant","n":"Arrogant","kd":"M","s":"Likes to dominate his opponent, challenge the most powerful foe in combat."},{"k":"bad_eyes","n":"Bad Eyes","kd":"M/m","s":"–1 to all Trait rolls dependent on vision, or –2 as a Major Hindrance. Eyewear negates penalty but have a 50% chance of breaking when the hero suffers trauma.","f":"all rolls -1 (major -2) when vision matters"},{"k":"bad_luck","n":"Bad Luck","kd":"M","s":"The characters starts with one less Benny per session.","f":"bennies -1"},{"k":"big_mouth","n":"Big Mouth","kd":"m","s":"Unable to keep secrets and constantly gives away private information."},{"k":"blind","n":"Blind","kd":"M","s":"–6 to all tasks that require vision (but choice of a free Edge to offset).","f":"all rolls -6 when vision is needed"},{"k":"bloodthirsty","n":"Bloodthirsty","kd":"M","s":"Never takes prisoners."},{"k":"can_t_swim","n":"Can’t Swim","kd":"m","s":"–2 to swimming (Athletics ) rolls; swimming Pace is one yard per round.","f":"Athletics -2 when swimming"},{"k":"cautious","n":"Cautious","kd":"m","s":"The character plans extensively and/or is overly careful."},{"k":"clueless","n":"Clueless","kd":"M","s":"–2 to Common Knowledge and Notice rolls.","f":"Common Knowledge/Notice -2"},{"k":"clumsy","n":"Clumsy","kd":"M","s":"–2 to Athletics and Stealth rolls.","f":"Athletics/Stealth -2"},{"k":"code_of_honor","n":"Code of Honor","kd":"M","s":"The character keeps his word and acts like a gentleman."},{"k":"curious","n":"Curious","kd":"M","s":"The character wants to know about everything."},{"k":"death_wish","n":"Death Wish","kd":"m","s":"The hero wants to die after or while completing some epic task."},{"k":"delusional","n":"Delusional","kd":"M/m","s":"The individual believes something strange that causes him occasional or frequent trouble."},{"k":"doubting_thomas","n":"Doubting Thomas","kd":"m","s":"The character doesn’t believe in the supernatural, often exposing him to unnecessary risks."},{"k":"driven","n":"Driven","kd":"M/m","s":"The hero’s actions are driven by some important goal or belief."},{"k":"elderly","n":"Elderly","kd":"M","s":"Pace –1, Agility, Strength, and Vigor rolls –1, but hero gets 5 extra skill points.","f":"pace -1\nAgility rolls -1\nStrength rolls -1\nVigor rolls -1"},{"k":"enemy","n":"Enemy","kd":"M/m","s":"The character has a recurring nemesis."},{"k":"greedy","n":"Greedy","kd":"M/m","s":"The individual is obsessed with wealth and material possessions."},{"k":"habit","n":"Habit","kd":"M/m","s":"Addicted to something, suffers Fatigue if deprived."},{"k":"hard_of_hearing","n":"Hard of Hearing","kd":"M/m","s":"–4 to Notice sounds; automatic failure if completely deaf.","f":"Notice -2 (major -4) when listening for sounds"},{"k":"heroic","n":"Heroic","kd":"M","s":"The character always helps those in need."},{"k":"hesitant","n":"Hesitant","kd":"m","s":"Draw two Action Cards and take the lowest (except Jokers, which may be kept).","f":"initiative hesitant"},{"k":"illiterate","n":"Illiterate","kd":"m","s":"The character cannot read or write."},{"k":"impulsive","n":"Impulsive","kd":"M","s":"The hero leaps before he looks."},{"k":"jealous","n":"Jealous","kd":"M/m","s":"The individual covets what others have."},{"k":"loyal","n":"Loyal","kd":"m","s":"The hero is loyal to his friends and allies."},{"k":"mean","n":"Mean","kd":"m","s":"–1 to Persuasion rolls.","f":"Persuasion -1"},{"k":"mild_mannered","n":"Mild Mannered","kd":"m","s":"–1 to Intimidation rolls.","f":"Intimidation -1"},{"k":"mute","n":"Mute","kd":"M","s":"The hero cannot speak and subtracts 2 from rolls that require audible communication.","f":"all rolls -2 when speaking is needed"},{"k":"obese","n":"Obese","kd":"m","s":"Size +1, Pace –1 and running die of d4.","f":"pace -1\ntoughness +1"},{"k":"obligation","n":"Obligation","kd":"M/m","s":"The character has a weekly obligation of 20 (Minor) to 40 (Major) hours."},{"k":"one_arm","n":"One Arm","kd":"M","s":"–4 to tasks (such as Athletics) that require two hands.","f":"all rolls -4 when two hands are needed"},{"k":"one_eye","n":"One Eye","kd":"M","s":"–2 to actions at 5” (10 yards) or more distance.","f":"all rolls -2 when the target is 5\" (10 yards) or more away"},{"k":"outsider","n":"Outsider","kd":"M/m","s":"The character doesn’t fit in to the local environment and subtracts 1 from Persuasion rolls, or 2 as a Major Hindrance and has no legal rights or other serious consequences.","f":"Persuasion -1 (major -2)"},{"k":"overconfident","n":"Overconfident","kd":"M","s":"The hero believes she can do anything."},{"k":"pacifist","n":"Pacifist","kd":"M/m","s":"Fights only in self-defense as a Minor Hindrance, won’t fight at all as Major."},{"k":"phobia","n":"Phobia","kd":"M/m","s":"The character is afraid of something, and subtracts –1/–2 from all Trait rolls in its presence.","f":"all rolls -1 (major -2) when the phobia is present"},{"k":"poverty","n":"Poverty","kd":"m","s":"Half starting funds and the character is always broke."},{"k":"quirk","n":"Quirk","kd":"m","s":"The individual has some minor but persistent foible that often annoys others."},{"k":"ruthless","n":"Ruthless","kd":"M/m","s":"The character does what it takes to get her way."},{"k":"secret","n":"Secret","kd":"M/m","s":"The hero has a dark secret of some kind."},{"k":"shamed","n":"Shamed","kd":"M/m","s":"The individual is haunted by some tragic event from her past."},{"k":"slow","n":"Slow","kd":"M/m","s":"As Minor, Pace reduced by 1 and running die is a d4. As Major, Pace reduced by 2, running die is d4–1 (minimum 1), subtract 2 from Athletics and rolls to resist Athletics. May not take the Fleet-Footed Edge.","f":"pace -1 (major -2)\nAthletics +0 (major -2)"},{"k":"small","n":"Small","kd":"m","s":"Size and Toughness are reduced by 1.","f":"toughness -1"},{"k":"stubborn","n":"Stubborn","kd":"m","s":"The character wants his way and rarely admits his mistakes."},{"k":"suspicious","n":"Suspicious","kd":"M/m","s":"The individual is paranoid."},{"k":"thin_skinned","n":"Thin Skinned","kd":"M/m","s":"The character is particularly susceptible to personal attacks. As a Minor Hindrance, he subtracts two when resisting Taunt attacks. As a Major, he subtracts four.","f":"Smarts rolls -2 (major -4) when resisting Taunt"},{"k":"tongue_tied","n":"Tongue-Tied","kd":"M","s":"The character often misspeaks or can’t get her words out. –1 to Intimidation, Persuasion, and Taunt rolls.","f":"Intimidation/Persuasion/Taunt -1"},{"k":"ugly","n":"Ugly","kd":"M/m","s":"The character is physically unattractive and subtracts 1 or 2 from Persuasion rolls.","f":"Persuasion -1 (major -2)"},{"k":"vengeful","n":"Vengeful","kd":"M/m","s":"The adventurer seeks payback for slights against her. As a Major Hindrance, she’ll cause physical harm to get it."},{"k":"vow","n":"Vow","kd":"M/m","s":"The individual has pledged himself to some cause."},{"k":"wanted","n":"Wanted","kd":"M/m","s":"The character is wanted by the authorities."},{"k":"yellow","n":"Yellow","kd":"M","s":"–2 to Fear checks and resisting Intimidation.","f":"Spirit rolls -2 when resisting fear or Intimidation"},{"k":"young","n":"Young","kd":"M/m","s":"Common Knowledge is not a core skill. As a Major Hindrance, she’s also Small (Size and Toughness reduced by 1).","f":"toughness +0 (major -1)"},{"k":"alien_form","n":"Alien Form","kd":"M","s":"-4 charisma, healing -4, lots of RP problems","l":"Your character is completely alien in appearance: a glowing ball of energy, an amoeba with tentacles, a large floating brain, and so on. He suffers –4 to Charisma, and his physiology is nearly impossible for humanoids to figure out. Healing rolls made to help the hero are made at –4. Numerous roleplaying instances should also be a major challenge as well—he can’t get into restaurants, wear a flak jacket, fit into a car, and so on, as defined by his odd shape. Your alien’s form may grant him special perks, but these must be bought as powers. If a glowing ball of energy wants to be able to pass through walls, for example, take the intangibility power. In other words, if your character doesn’t have a power, his form doesn’t grant it to him “for free,” no matter how you describe it."},{"k":"allergy","n":"Allergy","kd":"M/m","s":"-2/-4 to all traits rolls when near substance","l":"Your character suffers an aversion to a common condition or substance, such as water, fire, cold, sunlight, etc. Exposure to that substance (generally within six feet of it) inflicts a –2 penalty to all your character’s Trait rolls as a Minor Hindrance. As a Major Hindrance, your hero suffers a –4 penalty to all Trait rolls and his Pace is halved. This continues while exposed and for 2d6 rounds after the substance is removed or shielded somehow.","f":"all rolls -2 (major -4) when near the substance"},{"k":"dependency","n":"Dependency","kd":"M","s":"must be in contact with the substance once per day","l":"The creature must consume or have contact with some sort of relatively common substance periodically. Creatures from water-based worlds, for example, might need to immerse themselves in water one hour out of every 24 while a vampire might need a pint of blood each night. If the character doesn’t have the required contact, she suffers Fatigue each day until Incapacitated. A day after that, she perishes. Each hour spent recovering with the appropriate substance restores a level of Fatigue."},{"k":"dependent","n":"Dependent","kd":"M","s":"a lois to your clark","l":"It may not be an intrepid reporter or a loyal butler, but your character has some person to which he is completely devoted and will do anything to protect. This may be his wife or girlfriend, one of his children, a minion, or even a pet. The Dependent is a Novice Rank character and, while scrappy in her own right, just isn’t up to par with the rest of the party. For whatever reason, this doesn’t stop the Dependent from getting involved—often. She constantly requires saving, reveals team secrets, or otherwise causes your champion no end of grief. Of course, every now and then, the friend might just save the hero’s life, but such instances should be rare. If the Dependent ever dies, your hero is grief-stricken until he gets reasonably permanent justice…or revenge! This might mean putting a villain in jail or—for a villain—defeating a hero in a painful and elaborate death trap. Justice doesn’t have to be truly permanent—just long and lasting rather than fleeting and temporary. Until then, the affected character receives only one Benny at the beginning of each game session (but Luck and other bonuses apply normally)."},{"k":"distinctive_appearance","n":"Distinctive Appearance","kd":"m","s":"you can not disguise yourself, because something about you stands out","l":"Your super’s appearance is somewhat different from others of his race (a blueskinned human, a talking gorilla, etc.), and is relatively easy to spot, even out of costume. This makes the character easier to track down and pick out of a crowd and can even cause troublesome social problems among his own people. The appearance must be present in and out of costume to count as a Hindrance—all supers are distinctive in costume."},{"k":"gimmick","n":"Gimmick","kd":"M","s":"shazam!","l":"Your character must change clothes, get angry, drink blood, summon mystical energy, swallow a pill or potion, or otherwise perform some task (taking at least one action) to access his powers—all his powers. Whatever the case, the hero can be prevented from using his powers if he cannot enact his “gimmick.” The hero cannot use any of his powers—or Edges or Traits bought with Power Points—without it. Two Characters: If your super hero transforms into a completely different person, both “characters” should be made separately, with the “normal” person created as a normal Novice character. Advances gained through play may be added to either form, but not both."},{"k":"monologuer","n":"Monologuer","kd":"M","s":"must save smarts at -2, or waste turn by gloating","l":"Some villains are known for gloating over their foes when they should be killing them, and some heroes can’t resist a chance to lecture or chastise evil-doers. Any time the character’s Action Card is a Club, he must make a Smarts roll at –2 or spend his action announcing his opponents’ doom, making excuses for his failures, reveling in his success, or scolding those around him for their misdeeds. The talkative character may only take free actions during his monologue."},{"k":"mania","n":"Mania","kd":"M/m","s":"mental illness, reduce Charisma by 2 to those who know of it","l":"The character has a serious and negative mental illness of some kind, such as the lack of empathy toward others or a psychopathic compulsion to cause harm. Both reduce Charisma by 2 to those who know of it. A Minor Mania occurs infrequently or isn’t often likely to get the character killed. A Major Mania is a more-or-less full time obsession with serious consequences if caught or discovered."},{"k":"out_of_my_league","n":"Out Of My League","kd":"m","s":"power limit in one power is 1/5 instead of 1/3","l":"A character with this Hindrance may not spend more than one fifth of his total Power Points in any one power (instead of the usual one-third). He still has the same number of points; they just have to be divided between more powers."},{"k":"power_negation","n":"Power Negation","kd":"M","s":"basically supermans kryptonite","l":"Exposure to a certain substance or condition robs your hero of all his super powers, including Edges and Traits bought with Power Points. Near contact with the substance causes the hero to make a Vigor roll each round. If the roll is failed, his Pace is reduced to 1 and he suffers Fatigue that can cause death. This continues while exposed and for 2d6 rounds after the substance is removed or shielded somehow. A level of Fatigue is recovered every minute after the substance is removed. The substance should be relatively uncommon or avoidable, such as gold, holy ground, or immersion in water. Very rare substances—chunks of your alien’s home planet, lotus flowers—are possible as well, but foes will eventually discover it."},{"k":"terminally_ill","n":"Terminally Ill","kd":"M","s":"face card = -1 to all traits, joker = you will die this session","l":"Your character suffers from a terminal and incurable illness and will die soon. At the beginning of every game session, draw a card. A face card means your hero’s symptoms are acting up this session. Whatever the specifics may be, he suffers a –1 penalty to all his Trait rolls this game. A Joker means your hero is about to die. At some point in the game session, preferably after accomplishing an important goal or an act of personal redemption, he dies. The Game Master should always give a dying hero a few last rounds of action to commit some noble sacrifice."},{"k":"weakness","n":"Weakness","kd":"M/m","s":"-4 to resist one power type. and +4/x2 damage from it","l":"Your character is more susceptible to a specific Power Type, such as ice and cold, fire and heat, radiation, magic, darkness, light, air, sound, and so on. He suffers +4 damage when hit by an attack of that type, or –4 to resist other types of effects. As a Major Hindrance, the hero or villain is incredibly vulnerable to the Power Type and should avoid it at all costs. He still resists at –4 but damage is doubled."}],SW_SKILLS=[["Academics","smarts",0],["Athletics","agility",1],["Battle","smarts",0],["Boating","agility",0],["Common Knowledge","smarts",1],["Driving","agility",0],["Electronics","smarts",0],["Faith","spirit",0],["Fighting","agility",0],["Focus","spirit",0],["Gambling","smarts",0],["Hacking","smarts",0],["Healing","smarts",0],["Intimidation","spirit",0],["Language","smarts",0],["Notice","smarts",1],["Occult","smarts",0],["Performance","spirit",0],["Persuasion","spirit",1],["Piloting","agility",0],["Psionics","smarts",0],["Repair","smarts",0],["Research","smarts",0],["Riding","agility",0],["Science","smarts",0],["Shooting","agility",0],["Spellcasting","smarts",0],["Stealth","agility",1],["Survival","smarts",0],["Taunt","smarts",0],["Thievery","agility",0],["Weird Science","smarts",0]];
